{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01042 - MONDO_17327",
  "verbalization": "Melphalan, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Primary Non-gestational Choriocarcinoma Of Ovary through a chain of indications involving Altretamine. The evidence suggests that Melphalan may be used in the treatment of various ovarian tumors, including Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary and Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary, all of which are indicated to be treated with Altretamine. This indicates a potential pathway where Melphalan is used in conjunction with Altretamine to target specific ovarian malignancies. The shared use of Altretamine in these contexts suggests a possible mechanism of action or therapeutic relationship between Melphalan and the disease, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible role for Melphalan in the treatment of this condition, though further research is needed to clarify the underlying biological interactions.",
